<%# `role="status"` makes the banner a polite live region. On the pages that
    morph on redirect-to-self — Today, the board — the sentence is inserted
    into a page that is already loaded, so a screen reader announces it, and
    it is the only account of what happened that anyone gets who can't see
    the row animate away (D-row-send-off). On a full page load a live region
    present at load time is not announced; that's a browser rule, not
    something to work around here. %>
<div class="mb-6 space-y-2">
  <% messages.each do |type, style, message| %>
    <div role="status"
         class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-sm <%= style %>">
      <span class="min-w-0 flex-1"><%= message %></span>
      <% if follow_up && type == "notice" %>
        <%= link_to follow_up["label"], follow_up["url"], class: "shrink-0 font-medium underline-offset-2 hover:underline" %>
      <% end %>
      <% if undo && type == "notice" %>
        <%= button_to undo["label"], undo["url"], method: undo_method,
              class: "btn btn-secondary btn-sm", form_class: "shrink-0" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
